name        = "[Shine] Lifeform Picker"
source_dir  = "."
output_dir  = "output"
description = [=[mod id 3787803421

[b]A Shine extension that lets aliens call their lifeform before the round starts.[/b]

Open the scoreboard during the pre-round, click the lifeform icon on your own row, and pick what you intend to play. Your pick shows on the scoreboard for your team and for spectators.

[b]It has no gameplay effect at all.[/b] Nothing is reserved, gated, or forced — you still evolve exactly as normal. It only replaces "who's going fade" in voice chat with something the whole team can read at a glance.

[h1]How to use it[/h1]

[list]
[*] Join the alien team during the pre-round.
[*] Hold the scoreboard key. Every alien has a lifeform icon on their row, defaulting to Skulk.
[*] Click [b]your own[/b] icon. A menu opens at your cursor: Skulk, Gorge, Lerk, Fade, Onos.
[*] Pick one. Every alien and spectator sees it immediately.
[/list]

The icons appear only before the round starts, and disappear the moment it begins. All picks are cleared for the next round.

[h1]Who sees what[/h1]

[list]
[*] [b]Aliens[/b] — see all picks, can declare.
[*] [b]Spectators[/b] — see all picks, cannot declare.
[*] [b]Marines[/b] — see nothing. Picks are filtered on the server, so the data never reaches a marine's machine at all rather than being sent and merely hidden.
[/list]

[h1]Requirements[/h1]

[list]
[*] Requires [b]Shine[/b]. It installs as a normal Shine extension and is enabled by default; toggle it with [i]sh_loadplugin lifeformpicker[/i].
[*] Must be run on the server. Clients need the mod too, since the icons and the pick menu are client-side.
[/list]

[h1]Compatibility[/h1]

Works alongside scoreboard mods such as Shimizu Scoreboard. Most of them claim lua/GUIScoreboard.lua outright; this one never touches the file, and instead patches the scoreboard's methods at runtime, so it layers on top instead of competing.

Note that Shimizu Scoreboard has a lifeform selector of its own. Running both gives you two sets of icons — pick one.

[h1]Credits[/h1]

The idea, and the click-your-icon-for-a-menu interaction, come from Hatta's discontinued [i]Shine - Lifeform Selector[/i]. The lifeform artwork is from Shimizu Scoreboard. This is an independent implementation rather than a fork of either.

Source: https://github.com/Bleuitup/Shine-Lifeform-Picker]=]
